[size=6][b]✦ Fairer Weapon and Magic Experience Gain[/b][/size]

Experience that follows what you actually do. In vanilla Morrowind every successful cast teaches the same and every hit teaches the same, so the fastest way to learn is a 1-magicka spell or a dagger jab, repeated a thousand times, and the big spells and heavy weapons you actually fight with teach no more than that. Here:

[b]Magic[/b]

[list]
[*][b]Costly spells teach more.[/b] Anything up to 15 magicka teaches exactly as in vanilla; above that a cast teaches in step with its cost, up to [b]5x[/b] for a spell of 75 magicka or more.
[*][b]A miscast still teaches[/b] a third of what the cast would have - up to the skill's next level, never over it: that takes a cast that works. Running out of magicka is not a miscast, and teaches nothing.
[*][b]Conjured gear teaches Conjuration.[/b] A hit with a bound weapon, a hit taken on a piece of bound armor and a block with a bound shield teach Conjuration a third of what they teach their own skill, on top of it.
[*][b]Shield spells teach Alteration.[/b] A hit taken under a shield spell teaches Alteration a third of a vanilla hit's worth - as long as it is the kind that shield wards off: a weapon or a claw under [b]Shield[/b] (a third of what it teaches your armor), fire under [b]Fire Shield[/b], frost under [b]Frost Shield[/b], shock under [b]Lightning Shield[/b].
[/list]

[b]Weapons[/b]

[list]
[*][b]Slow weapons teach more per hit.[/b] How long the weapon's weakest swing takes - the attack animation the game plays for it, at its speed, wind-up to follow-through - decides it: half a second of it teaches one vanilla hit, three quarters of a second for ranged weapons. A dagger teaches less than vanilla, a two-handed axe about a third more.
[*][b]Strong attacks teach a third more.[/b] An attack wound up all the way teaches a third more than the weakest one, and in between in step with how far you wound it up.
[*][b]A miss still teaches[/b] a fifth of what the hit would have - a real miss, where the swing reached its target, and up to the skill's next level, never over it: that takes a hit. A swing at the air teaches nothing.
[/list]

Developed for OpenMW. [b]Requires OpenMW 0.51+[/b] and [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/morrowind/mods/60256]Max Yari's Script Services[/url].

[url=https://ko-fi.com/maxyari][img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/MaxYari/ArcanePracticeOpenMW/main/imgs/morrowind_kofi_banner_left_half_bright124.gif[/img][/url][url=https://ko-fi.com/maxyari][img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/MaxYari/ArcanePracticeOpenMW/main/imgs/nexus/banner_right.png[/img][/url]
[url=https://ko-fi.com/maxyari][img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/MaxYari/ArcanePracticeOpenMW/main/imgs/nexus/banner_glow.png[/img][/url]

[size=5][b]✦ How much more[/b][/size]

What a successful cast teaches, for some vanilla spells (their cost in brackets):

[list]
[*][b]1x[/b], as vanilla - Fireball (5), Fire Bite (6), Greater Fireball (10), Shield (15), and anything cheaper
[*][b]1.7x[/b] - Firebloom (26)
[*][b]2.3x[/b] - Lightning Storm (34)
[*][b]3x[/b] - Fire Shield (45)
[*][b]5x[/b] - God's Fire (135), Tap Energy (180), and anything else from 75 up
[/list]

What a typical weapon hit teaches, from the weakest attack to one wound up all the way:

[list]
[*][b]0.62x - 0.83x[/b] - daggers
[*][b]0.69x - 0.92x[/b] - short swords, staves
[*][b]0.8x - 1.07x[/b] - bare fists, knuckledusters
[*][b]0.89x - 1.19x[/b] - katars (Katars and Knuckledusters), thrown weapons
[*][b]1.03x - 1.37x[/b] - claymores
[*][b]1.15x - 1.53x[/b] - one-handed long swords
[*][b]1.2x - 1.6x[/b] - maces, spears
[*][b]1.24x - 1.65x[/b] - one-handed axes
[*][b]1.29x - 1.72x[/b] - two-handed axes, warhammers
[*][b]1.87x - 2.49x[/b] - bows; [b]2.04x - 2.72x[/b] - crossbows
[/list]

The swing lengths were measured from [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/morrowind/mods/52596]ReAnimation[/url]'s animations, and the mod uses them whatever animations you have; vanilla's are close.

[b]Won't leveling fly by once I can cast the big spells?[/b]
[spoiler]

No. Between 15 and 75 magicka, every spell teaches the same for the magicka it costs, so what you learn from a full bar of magicka is the same whichever spells you spend it on - and each point of a skill takes a little more experience than the one before it (skill + 1, times your major/minor multiplier), while your magicka grows much more slowly than that. Casting the best spell you can reliably cast, a point of a major skill takes about one full bar at skill 20, three at 40, four at 60 and eleven at 100. In vanilla, the same spells would take one, eight, twenty-three and sixty-two.

What changes is that the spells you fight with are no longer the slow way to learn. A 1-magicka spell cast over and over still teaches as much as it does in vanilla.

[/spoiler]

[size=5][b]✦ How to install[/b][/size]

[b]Requires OpenMW 0.51+[/b]

[list=1]
[*]Install [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/morrowind/mods/60256]Max Yari's Script Services[/url] if you don't have it yet.
[*]Install this mod [b]with a mod organiser[/b]: download the archive and drag and drop it into your mod organiser of choice (e.g [url=https://github.com/ModOrganizer2/modorganizer/releases]Mod Organizer 2[/url] on Windows or [url=https://github.com/grazelandsnomad/nerevarine_organizer/releases/tag/v0.70]Nerevarine Organizer[/url] on Linux). [b]Or[/b]: [url=https://modding-openmw.com/tips/installing-mods/]read this tutorial[/url] on how to install mods using the launcher or completely manually (it's also very easy).
[*]Enable [font=Courier New]FairerWeaponAndMagicXP.omwscripts[/font] in the "Content Files" tab of the OpenMW launcher, after [font=Courier New]MaxYariScriptServices.omwscripts[/font].
[/list]

It can be added to or removed from a game in progress at any time. It adds nothing to your save.

[size=5][b]✦ Settings[/b][/size]

Options -> Scripts -> Fairer Weapon and Magic Experience Gain. Every number above is a setting:

[list]
[*][b]Magic[/b]: the cost that teaches as vanilla (15), the cost of a top spell (75), the most a cast can teach (5x), and the three shares - miscast (0.33), conjured gear (0.33) and shield (0.33).
[*][b]Weapons[/b]: the seconds of a weapon's weakest swing that teach a vanilla hit, melee (0.5) and ranged (0.75), the full-strength bonus (0.33), and misses (0.2).
[/list]

A share of 0 turns that part off. "Log experience" (on) writes a line to the console (F10) and openmw.log for every bit of experience the mod gives or changes: which skill, how much, what for, and every multiplier with its reason.

[size=5][b]✦ Mod compatibility[/b][/size]

Fairer Weapon and Magic Experience Gain hands every gain to the game's own skill progression, so mods that change how skills level up - uncappers, level-up overhauls - see it as they would any other experience. It does no work per frame beyond reading one flag.

[list]
[*][b]Other mods that scale magic or weapon experience[/b] - MBSP, Skill Uses Scaled, NCGDMW's magicka-based progression: use one or the other, or both scale the same experience.
[*][b]Other mods that give experience for miscasts[/b] - Failed Spell Progress, FailureXP: set "Miscast experience" to 0 here, or turn theirs off.
[*][b][url=https://github.com/MaxYari/Katars-KnucklesOpenMW]Katars and Knuckledusters[/url][/b]: katars and knuckledusters swing with the hand-to-hand animations, and are measured that way. Bound Fist teaches Conjuration too, and a miss is split between Hand to Hand and the weapon skill as Katars splits a hit.
[*][b][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/morrowind/mods/58693]Unofficial Tamriel Rebuilt Spells[/url][/b] and Tamriel Rebuilt: their bound weapons and armor count, scaled ones included.
[*][b]Oblivion-Style Spell Casting / Spell Framework Plus[/b]: not tried. They cast in their own way, so miscasts made through them teach nothing here.
[/list]

